From: Vyron Code D-11 local hardening (VYRON_CODE_COMPLETE_LOCAL_HERMES_D11_DELIVERY_AUTHORIZATION)
Applies to: NousResearch/hermes-agent, installed local copy (confirmed present, unchanged, in
the current official upstream `main` branch as of this writing too — see
VYRON_CODE_V02_D11_AUTH_AND_EPHEMERAL_HISTORY_DISCOVERY_REPORT.md for the evidence trail).

OPTIONAL, NOT APPLIED. This patch was not applied to your installed Hermes Agent — this
development environment's own permission system blocks writes to files outside this
repository, so it was never attempted against your real installation, by design (no
work-around was attempted). This file exists so you can review, and optionally apply, the
exact change yourself.

WHAT IT DOES:
  1. (Redundant with scripts/hermes-auth-proxy.mjs, included for completeness/correctness if
     you'd rather fix it at the source): adds an `Authorization: Bearer <API_SERVER_KEY>`
     check to `POST /v1/chat/completions` and `POST /v1/responses`, identical in spirit to the
     existing `@_require_auth` decorator already used elsewhere in the same file for
     `/v1/models` and the response-management routes.
  2. (Not achievable any other way found this task): sets `agent._persist_disabled = True`
     immediately after agent construction in `_create_agent`, reusing the exact mechanism
     `background_review.py` already uses today for its own persistence-isolated forked agents.
     This prevents the session/history/message durable write that otherwise happens
     unconditionally on every `api_server` task request.

HOW TO APPLY (PowerShell, run as the same user who owns the Hermes installation):
  1. Back up first (belt-and-suspenders on top of this patch's own git-apply safety):
       Copy-Item "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\gateway\platforms\api_server.py" "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\gateway\platforms\api_server.py.bak"
       Copy-Item "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\gateway\platforms\api_server_openai_routes.py" "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent\gateway\platforms\api_server_openai_routes.py.bak"
  2. From this repository root:
       git apply --directory="$env:LOCALAPPDATA\hermes\hermes-agent" hermes-patches/0001-api-server-task-auth-and-ephemeral-history.patch
     (or apply the two hunks below by hand if `git apply` complains about line-ending/path
     differences against your installed copy's exact version.)
  3. Restart Hermes: `hermes gateway run` (after stopping any existing instance).
  4. Re-run `scripts/hermes-auth-proxy.mjs` is then optional — Hermes itself now enforces auth,
     so Vyron Code can point directly at Hermes's own port again instead of the proxy port.

HOW TO ROLL BACK:
  Restore the two `.bak` files created in step 1, or re-run your own package
  install/repair/reinstall for Hermes Agent 0.21.0.

